<title>USA: Norton McNaughton Inc Q2 loss widens.</title>
<headline>Norton McNaughton Inc Q2 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thirteen Weeks Ended  Twenty-Six Weeks Ended</p>
<p>				May 3,     May 4,   May 3,     May 4,</p>
<p>				   1997     1996	1997	1996</p>
<p>			   (In Thousands, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p> Net sales		  $52,873   $57,439  $94,469    $99,846</p>
<p> Loss from operations   (5,925)     (703)  (5,629)	(818)</p>
<p> Net loss		(3,551)(a)     (736) (3,508)(a)  (1,016)</p>
<p>Per Share Data:</p>
<p> Net loss		 (0.47)(a)    (0.09) (0.46)(a)    (0.13)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>common shares and common</p>
<p>stock equivalents</p>
<p>  outstanding		 7,489     7,792    7,563	7,898</p>
<p>(a) Includes the effect of a special pretax charge of about $5.7 million, or $0.44 per share on an after tax basis, in connection with severance payments resulting from management changes, the termination of lease obligations and the establishment of reserves for contingencies, including the anticipated closing of the Norty's retail stores.</p>
<p>Excluding these charges, the losses for the quarter and twenty-six week periods would have been $0.03 for each.</p>
</text>
